        "cost_rule_ref": "ONX_JDP_IID_GAP_res_d2c365d4eb",
        "display_label_zh": "Scalar reward of the selected action"
      },
      "target_object_registry": [
        {
          "id": "ONX_JDP_IID_GAP_obj_266f1fd9a2",
          "type": "online_environment",
          "definition": "Contexts $x_t$ are sampled independently from an unknown distribution $P$. The finite action set $\\mathcal A$ and feature map $\\phi$ are public. The fixed unknown parameter and features lie in the Euclidean unit ball: $$\\|\\phi(x,a)\\|_2\\le1,\\quad\\|\\theta_\\star\\|_2\\le1,\\quad Y_t\\in[-1,1],\\quad\\mathbb E[Y_t\\mid x_t,a_t,\\mathcal H_{t-1}]=\\langle\\phi(x_t,a_t),\\theta_\\star\\rangle.$$ Rewards are fresh draws from the current conditional distribution. The context is observed before choosing an action; its reward is revealed afterwards. Define $f^\\star(x,a)=\\langle\\phi(x,a),\\theta_\\star\\rangle$. Optimal actions may tie, but every suboptimal action has the same uniform positive-gap lower bound: $$a\\notin\\operatorname*{arg\\,max}_{b\\in\\mathcal A}f^\\star(x,b)\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\max_{b\\in\\mathcal A}f^\\star(x,b)-f^\\star(x,a)\\ge\\Delta_{\\min}>0.$$"
        }
      ],
